<h2>How to buy tickets online and what happens next: delivery and entry</h2>
<p>Delivery depends on the event and seller. This part of how to buy tickets online is about delivery. Our buyer protection page lists electronic delivery, mobile transfer and physical shipping as possible methods, and says tickets will arrive before the event. Some tickets are released closer to the event date, based on organizer timing, so a ticket that has not arrived right away is not always a problem. If tickets do not arrive in time, our support team assists you.</p>
<p>Most events accept mobile tickets, and printing is only needed if the event page says so. On the day, bring your ticket and a government-issued ID if the venue requires one. The <a href="/ticket-faq">ticket FAQ</a> covers entry rules, age limits and what you can bring. For a general explanation of digital tickets, see <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile_ticketing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mobile ticketing on Wikipedia</a>.</p>

<h2>Safe habits for how to buy tickets online</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Only enter payment details on a page you reached from the site itself.</li>
  <li>Read the refund and cancellation terms on the event page before you pay.</li>
  <li>Keep confirmation emails and screenshots of your order, as any guide on how to buy tickets online will suggest.</li>
  <li>Be wary of anyone who asks you to pay outside the checkout.</li>
</ul>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission offers further <a href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/online-shopping" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tips for shopping online</a>. On our side, the <a href="/ticket-buyer-protection">ticket buyer protection page</a> says orders are covered for valid tickets, delivery before the event, secure payment processing and support. If an event is canceled and not rescheduled, you receive a full refund. Most other tickets are non-refundable unless the event is canceled or postponed, so check before you buy. Read the <a href="/worry-free-guarantee">worry-free guarantee</a> for the full wording.</p>
